        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David J. Wineland, Serge Haroche\n- Organizations: National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST)\n- Awards: 2012 Nobel Prize in Physics\n- Topics: quantum systems, photons\n\nFacts:\n- David J. Wineland was born on February 24, 1944, and is an American physicist at the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) physics laboratory.\n- Serge Haroche was born on 11 September 1944 and is a French physicist.\n- David J. Wineland and Serge Haroche were jointly awarded the 2012 Nobel Prize in Physics for ground-breaking experimental methods that enable measuring and manipulation of individual quantum systems.\n- Serge Haroche's Nobel-recognized work included the study of the particle of light, the photon.",
